From: Noxwell <beebono@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-ufs: add SM4450 UFS PHY

Add the SM4450 (parrot/ravelin) UFS PHY with QMP v5 register layout, two
lanes, up to HS-G4. The host powers the PHY up in its maximum gear, so
G4 must be accepted even when the attached device is slower.

The init sequence is the downstream parrot one, split into a common
table and per-gear overlays (G3 for HS-G1..G3, G4) so that each gear
gets exactly the writes of the matching downstream calibration table.
It only differs from sm8350 in the TX res code lane offsets and, for
G3 and below, the PCS gear capability and 20us timer settings.

Ported from downstream phy-qcom-ufs-qmp-v4-parrot.{c,h}:
https://github.com/cupid-development/android_kernel_xiaomi_sm8450/blob/060fed194023de6ed41cb25e9a15cfa307b05469/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-ufs-qmp-v4-parrot.h

